From b4a41d2817ce152a1932b7ada1f68db78da47bc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:53:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add gamepad input layer and virtual cursor fallback

Adds controller support plumbing to the shared input loop:

- GamePadInput (UpdateState.Pad): polls the first connected pad, applies a
  rescaled radial stick dead zone and trigger dead zone, and exposes
  press/release/auto-repeat edges for semantic PadActions plus combined
  D-pad/left-stick navigation.
- PadBindings: default action->button map, optional confirm/cancel swap,
  and overrides from a plain-text gamepad.ini in the user directory.
- PointerDeviceTracker (UpdateState.LastInputDevice): whichever of mouse or
  pad was used most recently drives the pointer. Ignores the OS echoing a
  cursor warp, small jitter, and the zeroed mouse state while unfocused.
- VirtualCursor: while the pad is the active device, the left stick drives
  a stand-in mouse cursor (A/X/Y = left/right/middle, triggers = wheel,
  B = Escape) and the OS cursor is warped to match, so every existing
  screen is usable with a pad before it gets native navigation.
- GlobalSettings: GamePadEnabled, GamePadVirtualCursor, GamePadDeadZone,
  GamePadCursorSpeed, GamePadSwapConfirmCancel; applied in GameFacade.Init.

Mouse and keyboard behaviour is unchanged while the pad is idle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
